= keep
- 52b298a69 Add a Gradle build for the JVM backend

= JVM: ASM 9.10.1, Java 25 bytecode, and a first Kotlin slice
ASM 4.1 becomes 9.10.1 (asm + asm-tree), compilation and the generated
bytecode target Java 25, and the io/ interfaces, Base64, Buffers, HLLConfig
and VMArrayInstance_i are the prototype Kotlin conversions that prove the
mixed-source build. stage0 regenerated for the new bytecode version.
- 134fe15d0 JVM: convert a prototype slice of the runtime to Kotlin
- b2cdedaa6 JVM: upgrade ASM 4.1 to 9.10.1
- 2d91e93fd JVM: target Java 25 for compilation and generated bytecode
- 90ab16c81 Bootstrap JVM backend

= JVM: convert IOOps, the async handles and ExceptionHandling to Kotlin
The VMArrayInstance_* and MultiDimArrayInstance_* REPR classes are now
generated from one buildSrc template. AsyncFileHandle gets its ops back
(openasync/spurtasync, plus slurpasync/linesasync), a test, and an
idiomatic rewrite, as does AsyncProcessHandle; docs/ops.markdown records
the ops. IOOps and ExceptionHandling become Kotlin objects with their
descriptors unchanged; stage0 re-pinned after the compiler change.
