= JVM: dependency sweep: lz4 safeInstance, fastutil, JNA 5.19.1, jline 4
lz4 uses its pure-Java safeInstance instead of the Unsafe fast path, heaps
are capped explicitly instead of -XX:+AggressiveHeap, fastutil 8.5.19,
JNA 5.19.1 with native access enabled, and interactive readline on jline 4.
Found on the way: nqp::where gets a null-safe identity and reading from a
tty no longer busy-spins.
# The JNA bump is superseded by the java.lang.foreign group below; it cannot
# be folded there (NativeCallOps and the C*Instance files are converted to
# Kotlin in between).
- e6d79aba0 JVM: use lz4's pure-Java safeInstance instead of the Unsafe fast path
- 701420aae JVM: cap heaps explicitly instead of -XX:+AggressiveHeap (Gradle path)
- ca922dd63 JVM: bump fastutil to 8.5.19 (Gradle path)
- 541a648aa JVM: modernize JNA to 5.19.1 and enable native access
- 8c45ad354 JVM: port interactive readline to jline 4
- 13dc0a0b0 JVM: give nqp::where a null-safe identity
- 6fbd79061 JVM: stop busy-spinning when reading from a tty

