= JVM: convert the long tail to Kotlin: NativeRef leaves, interop, jast2bc
The NativeRef variants and small instance leaves, the boxed array pair and
DecoderInstance, BootJavaInterop, JASTCompiler, IndyBootstrap and the
AutosplitMethodWriter (asm-tree on the runner classpath, autosplit test).
nqp hash values are modelled as nullable. eval returns the mainline's value
on both the JVM and js backends.
- 7a264de77 JVM: convert the NativeRef variants and small instance leaves to Kotlin
- 5aa808ae3 JVM: model nqp hash values as nullable
- 7733e4ac8 JVM: convert the boxed array pair, its bases, and DecoderInstance
- a43a169b7 JVM: convert BootJavaInterop to Kotlin
- 06a5add62 JVM: convert JASTCompiler to Kotlin
- 08de6d229 JVM: convert IndyBootstrap to Kotlin
- c2ef73bf3 JVM: put asm-tree on the runner classpath and test the autosplitter
- 2799cc816 JVM/js: make eval return the mainline's value
- f8d92602a JVM: convert AutosplitMethodWriter to Kotlin

= JVM: convert Ops to Kotlin
The generated-code ABI converted whole: object Ops with @JvmStatic on every
op, all public static descriptors javap-identical, every reference-typed
op parameter honestly nullable. BootJavaInterop.marshalOutRecursive is
emitted as a non-final static and ContainerSpec's cas/atomic_load returns
are honestly nullable, both needed by the org.raku.rakudo layer conversion.
- 34b9b7d38 JVM: convert Ops to Kotlin
- 7442667ed JVM: emit BootJavaInterop.marshalOutRecursive as a non-final static
- 3d5c88acd JVM: make ContainerSpec cas/atomic_load returns honestly nullable

= docs: the Kotlin migration notes, round by round
Findings and final conclusions of the conversion rounds: S3 and the
nullability cluster, the invokeExact trap, the dependency sweep and its REPL
discoveries, the medium runtime classes, C interop and the planned
post-parity !! cleanup, the long-tail rounds, the autosplitter and eval
return value, the Ops conversion, and the org.raku.rakudo layer.
