= JVM: dodge HotSpot's 65535-indy-per-class cliff
The wval index is pushed as an int plus i2l rather than a long constant,
so it stops eating constant-pool entries.
- bbb5bcac3 JVM: dodge HotSpot's 65535-indy-per-class cliff
- d7c64c053 JVM: push wval index as int + i2l, not a long constant

= keep
