= JVM: batch static lexical setup so the core setting fits a class
The fixes that got Rakudo's core setting through the JVM backend: a
fragment only carries the locals it uses, contvar declarations with local
scope, a re-referenced block keeps its args expectation, every code ref in
the table gets a method, the tasks hanging off a parameter run, a REPR can
force an STable it depends on, ctxcallerskipthunks skips compiler stubs,
errors say what actually went wrong, and HLL::Compiler no longer silently
skips a stage that threw.
